[center][size=6][b]Eve (Stellar Blade) v1.2.0-ANIMTEST[/b][/size]
Experimental idle animation preview[/center]

[size=4][b]Added[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]14 additional selectable Eve idle animations, alongside Eve Default Idle, for 15 Eve choices in total.
[*]Make the new idle choices available across all six included outfits.
[*]Include standing, kneeling, seated, reclining and stretching poses. Choose them in CSS > LOCOMOTION > Idle Animation.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Changed[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Hide weapons during the custom idle poses, using CSS's existing idle controls.
[*]Keep the six v1.2.0 outfits, palettes, customization, physics assets and existing movement animations.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Fixed[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Adjust idle height placement, including the brief lift in Eve Seated Tuck.
[/list]

[b]Animation test build[/b]
The animations work in the author's in-game trial, but this is an experimental preview. Some clipping, pose transitions and ground contact still need polish. Every animation, outfit and combat interruption combination has not been exhaustively checked.

[size=4][b]Upgrading[/b][/size]
Requires Custom Shell System (CSS) with outfit-specific idle animation support. Close the game, back up your existing CSS_EveStellarBlade_eins0fx_P folder, then replace it with the folder from this ZIP under MortalShell2/Content/Paks/~mods/.

Keep the .pak, .ucas and .utoc files together. Do not install this alongside another Eve package or the old separate outfit trials. This Eve package does not need a separate CSS_SharedAssets_P installation; other mods may still need that package.

This download contains the same package tested in game. Its embedded version remains 1.2.0; ANIMTEST identifies this experimental download. Keep the original v1.2.0 download if you want to roll back.
